    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0362" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7557</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-03T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 3, 1917, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received November 4, 10 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1177. My 1175. Any promise of troops we might make would, of course, be
                    contingent on Italy’s fighting with all her might for herself. General Pershing can get exact situation from
                        Generals Robertson and Foch, who have been on the ground. I believe
                    Italian Government would rather have our declaration of war against Austria than
                    our troops.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
